  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Rune Armour" id="96ee-79a8-217a-28a7" hidden="false">
      <description>A model wearing rune armour has a 4+ invulnerable saving throw. If the model is mounted on a jetbike it may take either the normal 3+ armour saving throw or a 4+ rune armour invulnerable save.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Warp Jump Generators" id="0943-8bb7-8cc4-65f6" hidden="false">
      <description>A model with a Warp Jump Generator may moves up to 12" in the movement phase, ignoring all terrain during the move, but may not finish the move in impassable terrain. 
The unit may make a second jump at the start of the assault phase. They cannot use this jump and charge into combat in the same turn. This second jump moves 2D6" in a nominated direction, and if a double is rolled one member of the squad is removed as a casualty.
The unit also advanced and falls back 3D6" after close combat, ignoring terrain as normal.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Surprise Assault" id="88b7-c132-ffed-9f07" hidden="false">
      <description>When the Exarch and his squad charge, they gain +2 Attacks instead of the normal +1.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Withdraw" id="881b-e3fe-4cf9-4cb7" hidden="false">
      <description>If the Exarch's squad is in close combat at the end of the assault phase, they may fall back to take them out of combat if they wish. All normal rules for a fall back move apply, but the enemy squad may only make a 3" move to consolidate. The Exarch's unit automatically regroups after the fall back move.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Crushing Blow" id="6570-8481-1f30-3414" hidden="false">
      <description>The Exarch works out all close combat attacks at +1 Strength.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Stealth" id="cdd4-2891-a528-932c" hidden="false">
      <description>A squad led by this Exarch may infiltrate if allowed by the mission.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Acrobatic" id="63bf-dd8b-7daf-793f" hidden="false">
      <description>Before the Exarch makes her close combat attacks, she may be repositioned in contact with any model of your choice in the enemy unit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="War Shout" id="ed74-db03-79f2-e033" hidden="false">
      <description>When the Exarch charges into combat, during the first round of combat the enemy unit must pass a Leadership test or reduce its WS by -1 for the rest of the assault phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Banshee Masks" id="5e2c-19ac-6764-63d6" hidden="false">
      <description>Models wearing a Banshee Mask always strikes first in hand-to-hand combat in the first round of any assault, regardless of Initiative or other factors. This applies even if they are not in base contact with the enemy. The mask has no effect in additional rounds of combat. In the case of other effects that would allow their enemy to also strike first, both units strike simultaneously.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Burning Fist" id="ee49-4aa5-13d1-3530" hidden="false">
      <description>In close combat the Exarch may re-roll any failed wound rolls and ignores all armour saves.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Tank Hunter" id="a907-15db-1615-4b1b" hidden="false">
      <description>The Exarch may re-roll any armour penetration rolls he makes for shooting or in close combat against targets with an armour value.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Wraithsight" id="59d1-dec4-4d80-b9cc" hidden="false">
      <description>At the start of every Eldar turn, roll a D6 for each Wraithguard unit that is not joined by a Farseer or Warlock. On a roll of a 1, the Wraithguard may do nothing that turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Difficult Terrain" id="61b3-599d-af54-c39c" hidden="false">
      <description>Rangers moving through difficult terrain can roll one additional dice when determining their movement distance.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Cameleoline Cloaks" id="6755-7b76-b6aa-3214" hidden="false">
      <description>Rangers add +1 to any cover saves it is allowed (e.g. a 5+ cover save becomes a 4+ cover save). If not cover, they are granted a 6+ cover save.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Distract" id="ab65-4fb9-465e-a84e" hidden="false">
      <description>One model in base contact with the Exarch, chosen by the Eldar player, is at -1 Attacks. This can reduce the model to 0 Attacks.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Defend" id="3186-1d76-fabf-38c4" hidden="false">
      <description>If the Exarch chooses, he may force enemy models to only hit him on a roll of 6 in close combat, but by doing so he must strike last.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Skillful Rider" id="62c2-695f-6a13-1167" hidden="false">
      <description>The Exarch and his squad do not roll for difficult terrain.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Evade" id="be4c-fcc1-62c1-694b" hidden="false">
      <description>The Exarch's armour saving throw becomes an invulnerable saving throw.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Swooping Hawk Wings" id="6006-f98b-12ab-f1d5" hidden="false">
      <description>A model with Swooping Hawk Wings moves as if equipped with a jump pack. Additionally, a squad with Swooping Hawk Wings may always Deep Strike even if the mission does not normally allow.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Bounding Leap" id="43a2-6d53-eb4a-3729" hidden="false">
      <description>When making an assault move, the Exarch may add +D6" to the distance he charges. The Exarch may only charge if he is within 6" of the enemy in the assault phase, but he does not have to engage the first model in his path if this extra distance would allow him to reach another model.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Sustained Assault" id="79e6-8a77-2a4b-16a4" hidden="false">
      <description>For each close combat hit the Exarch makes, he may make an extra attack. These extra attacks, if they hit, allow him to make additional extra attacks.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Implacable Advance" id="d468-2107-0e7e-86e1" hidden="false">
      <description>Wraithlords can shoot up to two weapons if it moves, and all of its weapons if it stays stationary. It can even fire heavy weapons whilst moving.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Eldar Energy Field" id="7c2f-b369-5f7f-da26" hidden="false">
      <description>Any ranged attacks against the vehicle's front and side armour with a Strength greater than 8 counts as Strength 8. Additionally, all front and side attacks may only ever roll +1d6 for their armour penetration (for example, negating the Melta and Ordnance rules). Attacks in close combat or in the rear armour ignore this rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Weapons Platform" id="33f8-141c-6263-dfc6" hidden="false">
      <description>The support weapon has two Guardians as crew. One crewman fires the support weapon and the other is free to fire his own weapon. If both crew are killed the platform is useless (the platform itself can't be hit). Unlike other anti-grav platforms, the support weapon may not fire if it was moved in the movement phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Fast Shot" id="f63e-9b57-1074-ef2a" hidden="false">
      <description>If the Exarch is firing an assault or heavy weapon, add +1 to the number of shots fired. If instead firing a pistol or rapid fire weapon, then they do not count as moving. Fast Shot may not be used by the Exarch in the same turn as Crack Shot.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Crack Shot" id="f2fd-294c-434c-acdb" hidden="false">
      <description>The enemy may not making cover saves against shots from the Exarch, and the Exarch may re-roll any failed wound rolls when shooting. Crack Shot may not be used in the same turn the Exarch uses Fast Shot.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Runes of Warding" id="b5d1-5696-e960-ab8c" hidden="false">
      <description>If an enemy psyker attempts to use a psychic power and the psyker or the target is with 6" of the Farseer, the enemy must take the Psychic test on a 3D6 and discard the lowest roll. Psykers who not normally need to make a Psyhich test are unaffected.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Runes of Witnessing" id="06eb-6b01-a486-9121" hidden="false">
      <description>A Farseer with runes of witnessing rolls 3D6 and discards the highest when taking a Psychic test. Note, you must use the two lowest dice, even in the case of two ones.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ghosthelm" id="0fa3-a6b7-33c2-32a4" hidden="false">
      <description>If the model suffers an attack from the Perils of the Warp he may ignore the attack on a D6 roll of 4+. In addition, any Daemon that is fighting the model in close combat halves (rounding up) its WS.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Spirit Stones" id="b0a6-57c6-99c8-7a34" hidden="false">
      <description>A psyker with a spirit stone can use two powers each turn instead of one, but they must be different powers.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Armour of Vaul" id="b544-c18c-b0cb-90a5" hidden="false">
      <description>Instead of an armour save, Arienal must pass an unmodified Leadership test in order to save against any hits she suffers. If the test is failed she loses a wound as normal. The Armour of Vaul is an invulnerable save.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Alean - The Steed of Khaine" id="8ab9-b5a4-c3e8-20d3" hidden="false">
      <description>Naudhu rides upon a Viper that has been built to allow him to fight from its back, much as Khaine rode to war on the legendary steed Alean. He fights in close combat in the same way as a Dreadnought. He may make a 6" assault move in the assault phase, providing he moved no more than 12" in the movement phase, otherwise he may only fight if assaulted.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Fleet of Foot" id="7a77-8498-1878-5086" hidden="false">
      <description>Eldar units with this rule may run instead of shooting in the shooting phase. Roll a D6. The score is the distance in inches the unit may move in the shooting phase. This move is not affected by difficult terrain.
The Avatar; vehicles; jetbikes; any model with a saving throw better than 4+ (with the exception of Dire Avengers, Howling Banshees; Fire Dragon Exarchs and Phoenix Lords); units contain anti-grav/support weapons; and Dark Reapers may never run.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Battle Fate" id="3e45-82de-f527-4b3c" hidden="false">
      <description>Asurmen's save is invulnerable</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Star Engines" id="14a9-0694-d982-b67d" hidden="false">
      <description>This vehicle may move 2D6" in a straight line during the shooting phase, instead of firing weapons. It may not use the Star Engines in the same turn that it embarks or disembarks transported units.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Vectored Engines" id="fd4f-e837-e39f-53b7" hidden="false">
      <description>The vehicle may re-roll any failed Difficult Terrain test.</description>
    </rule>
  <rule id="b4a6-acb9-a829-7904" name="Expert Pilots" hidden="false">
      <description>Re-roll failed Difficult Terrain tests during the movement phase.</description>
    </rule>
  <rule id="6ace-f869-9923-ae4a" name="Ranger Disruption" hidden="false">
      <description>For each Rangers or Path-finders unit in the army, roll a D6 on the Ranger Disruption table. Ranger Disruption only affects units on the tabletop, it does not affect units in reserve. Units which are vehicles or are inside a vehicle cannot be affected by Ranger Disruption.

A unit cannot be affected more than once, and if an inappropriate unit is randomly selected then simple randomly select another unit instead.

Roll a D6:
1 - No effect
2 - A random enemy unit on the table is taken off and must start in research instead.
3 - A random enemy unit on the table starts the battle pinned. If this unit is immune to pinning then this result has no effect.
4 - An enemy unit on the table, chosen by the Eldar player, is taken off and must start in reserve instead.
5 - A unit on the table, chosen by the Eldar player, starts the battle pinned. A unit immune to pinning cannot be chosen.
6 - The Rangers or Path-finders may shoot once at one enemy unit chosen by the Eldar player, regardless of range or line of sight. Resolve this before the battle starts and if the unit is pinned by this shooting, it will start the battle pinned.</description>
    </rule>
  <rule id="dd8e-942c-0776-47f5" name="Tactical Withdrawal" hidden="false">
      <description>Black Guardians that fall back due to casualties inflicted will not fally and must continue to fall back even if above half strength. Any squad removed from play in this way whilst still above half strength only counts for half the unit's victory points.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="023d-7d75-7e64-0801" name="Webway Strike" hidden="false">
      <description>At least half the units (rounding up) in any Ulthwe Strike Force must be kept in reserve and enter play through a Wraithgate as described below, regardless of mission. These units must be noted down before deployment. Regardless of the mission being played, any unit that carries a Wraithgate automatically begins on table following the usual deployment rules.

Ulthwe Strike Force troops that are falling back must do so towards the nearest Wraithgate if one has been placed. If they are unable to they will fall back as specified in the mission. If a model from a unit that is falling back passes through the Wraightgate the entire unit is removed from play as if they had left the table. If the only model left on the table carrying a Wraithgate is destroyed, the Wraithgate is placed wih the central hole over the spot where the model died.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
  <sharedSelectionEntries>
    <selectionEntry name="Avatar of the Bloody-Handed God" id="a4ef-a5f7-1009-a021" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="unit">
